From 7b9aac1118a6af556bbcbb0d6205efe6e8303454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:06:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay: field-rate deterministic clock (battles ran at
 half speed), Showdown happiness default 255, stage row pinned to the chosen
 location (v1.5.12)

- The v1.5.11 clock counted one VI field per main-loop pass; XD runs one
  pass per two fields in battle, so battles ran at half speed. The clock
  unit is now the SDK's own VI retrace count (0x804EAC54, 59.94 Hz in
  every mode), sampled only at the main loop's 'now' stamp right after
  the retrace-released end-of-frame wait, so the read cannot straddle the
  recompiler skew; every other site uses the cached value. Dual core is
  pinned off while the clock is on.
- Showdown imports assume maximum happiness; a 'Happiness: N' line is
  honoured on desktop and Android (was the species base value, so Return
  hit for a fraction of its power).
- When a battle location is chosen, XD's VS-setup stage row is pinned to
  the 'random' entry and its sprite blanked so the picker cannot
  contradict the host's choice; the per-frame record pokes still deliver
  the location.
- Logs: xd lines gain pf=, xdclk gains S/F/R/dn, cpu line gains
  xd_clock_v, corepolicy gains cpu_thread.
